# The Long Table on the season (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs"): what's going on, the way a farm hears it.
# Homely, attentive, a little too interested in you. Nothing is ever described.

conv table.host.season
for table:host, table:mother
when !table:crossed
topic "Does any news reach you out here?"
prio world
voice table

bind horde = news:horde
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by

node start
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:taken -> taken
  say? epilogue :: That people are leaving, now the cure's out. Queues at the checkpoints, the loudspeakers say. We aren't going. The farm was here before the roads, and it'll be here after.
  say? cure>=75 :: That the lab in {lab_town} is nearly there with its cure. Good for them. We've never needed much medicine out here. Fresh air and a good supper, that's ours.
  say? rain :: The rain, mostly. It's good for the garden, and it keeps people indoors. Come and sit by the stove, you're dripping on the step.
  say Not much reaches us, and we like it that way. The trucks, the weather, who's short of what. Tell us yours, though. Where have you been today, and who did you see?
  > @about Here and there. -> asked
  > @back0 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node horde
  say A big crowd of them went past near {bind:horde}, following the noise. They never come up our lane. They never have. Lucky, we say.
  say Are you walking that way tonight? On your own?
  > @no1 Not tonight. I'll go round. -> hub
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node taken
  say {bind:who} has {bind:took} now, we hear. Flags up, flags down, all season long. Nobody out here salutes anyone. We just wave at whoever comes up the lane.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node asked
  say Here and there. That's the best sort of place to be. Nobody knows to come looking for you in here and there, do they?
  > @back3 I suppose not. Something else, then. -> hub
